# Everything listed here is excluded from the build context — the snapshot of
# files sent to the Docker daemon before the build starts. Without this,
# node_modules alone is 126 MB of host-built binaries that would be copied in
# and then thrown away, because the image installs its own.

node_modules
npm-debug.log*

# Secrets. These must never be baked into an image: anyone who can pull the
# image can read them, and image layers keep a file even after a later layer
# deletes it. Pass them at run time with --env-file or the platform's env vars.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
serviceAccount*.json
firebase-adminsdk*.json

# Real user data. Avatars and meal photos belong on a mounted volume, not in
# the image.
uploads

# Not needed to serve the API.
test
*.test.js
.github
docs
*.md
!README.md

# Local noise.
.git
.gitignore
.DS_Store
coverage
*.log
.vscode
.idea
